<title>ROMANIA: Minor tremor in east Romania, no injuries reported.</title>
<headline>Minor tremor in east Romania, no injuries reported.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A minor earthquake shook eastern Romania on Thursday evening but no damage was reported, the country's Earth Physics Institute said.</p>
<p>It said the tremor, measuring an intensity of 3.7 on the Richter scale, occurred at 7:56 p.m. (1756 GMT) in the mountainous Vrancea region, 300 km (200 miles) northeast of the capital. The tremor was not felt in Bucharest.</p>
